<title>USA: Greenville, S.C. parking revs 5.55 pct yld in 2017.</title>
<headline>Greenville, S.C. parking revs 5.55 pct yld in 2017.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Keegan said Tuesday it had been awarded a $8.775 million Greenville, S.C., parking system revenue bonds offering, with a top yield of 5.55 percent in 2017.</p>
<p>The offering was priced on Monday, September 23.</p>
<p>The bonds are AMBAC insured and rated Aaa by Moody's Investors Service and AAA by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>The bonds are dated 9/1/1996 and due 6/1/1997-2012, 2017 and 2022.</p>
<p>The first coupon is 12/1/1996.</p>
<p>The bonds are callable 6/1/2006 at 100.00.</p>
<p>PRICING SCALE</p>
